  "author": "Jeremy Sherman",
  "description": "If the universe is aimless, how do selves and aims emerge? Why do living beings have aims when inanimate things do not? Current science encourages us to reject the ghost-in-the-machine explanation&#8212;that something called spirit, soul, mind, or will was somehow breathed into matter&#8212;and instead accept that selves are just matter, in aimless mechanistic motion like everything else. But what about life's many emergent qualities, the multifarious purposes that shape actual physical behavior",
